<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace Core\Shared\Contracts;

/**
 * Concern (Interface / Aware)
 *
 * Purpose:
 * - Defines a small, explicit contract to support a particular abstraction.
 * - Represents a specific capability or responsibility ("aware of something").
 *
 * Naming rules:
 * - Must be self-descriptive.
 * - Must end with "Aware".
 *   Examples:
 *   - SelectorAware
 *   - SearchAware
 *   - TenantAware
 *   - ActionCreateAware
 *
 * Location:
 * - Can live in Core\Shared\Contracts when it is truly shared.
 * - Can also live in a more specific sub-namespace when the concern belongs
 *   to a particular layer or concept.
 *
 *   Examples:
 *   - Core\Shared\Contracts\SelectorAware
 *   - Core\Shared\Contracts\Actions\ActionCreateAware
 *   - Core\Shared\Contracts\Actions\ActionUpdateAware
 *
 * Architectural notes:
 * - Interfaces are NOT required by default.
 * - They are introduced only when a specific use case or abstraction needs it.
 * - The decision to add an Aware interface is always contextual and discussible.
 * - Never add this layer "just in case".
 *
 * This is a design decision, not a technical necessity.
 */
interface {Concern}Aware
{
    /**
     * Describe the capability provided by this concern.
     *
     * @param  mixed  ...$arguments
     * @return mixed
     */
    public function {method}(...$arguments);
}